invariant: INV-5
file: pem_files.c
catches: pem_files_test
reason: the key call reads an EC PARAMETERS block and does not ask which
  curve it names, so secp384r1's parameters, or any 10 bytes of DER, pass
  above a P-256 key. The ruling admits prime256v1's alone
  (docs/decisions.md 131). test_key_parameters writes secp384r1's and a
  changed OID and requires CH_EINVAL.

--- old
    return pem_read_block(r, PEM_LABEL_EC_PARAMETERS, &w) &&
           x509_pem_parameters_are_p256(parameters, w.len) && pem_skip_line_breaks(r) == '\n';
--- new
    (void)x509_pem_parameters_are_p256;
    return pem_read_block(r, PEM_LABEL_EC_PARAMETERS, &w) && pem_skip_line_breaks(r) == '\n';
